  "id": "sudden-expansion-re100",
  "name": "Sudden expansion · Re=100",
  "category": "Separated flow benchmark",
  "description": "Symmetric 1:3 expansion, parabolic inlet, no-slip walls, refined steps; lower-wall reattachment diagnostic.",
  "capabilities": [
    "Workbench",
    "TwoD",
    "Editable",
    "Recirculation",
    "Reattachment",
    "Unvalidated"
  ],
  "expectations": {
    "closed_domain": false,
    "positive_streamwise_flow": false,
    "curved_boundary": false,
    "non_ideal_mesh_quality": false,
    "notes": "Related study: Fearn, Mullin & Cliffe (1990), Nonlinear flow phenomena in a symmetric sudden expansion. https://doi.org/10.1017/S0022112090001707 . This starter uses upstream full width h=1, Umax=1, Re=Umax*h/nu; inlet is 5h before the expansion, outlet 30h after it, downstream width 3h. This Reynolds convention and finite-domain outlet must be reconciled with the publication before comparing bifurcation thresholds. Measure both recirculation lengths and pressure drop; lower-wall signed-shear diagnostic is enabled. Symmetric initialization and a steady solve may remain on a symmetric branch; discovering asymmetric/unsteady branches requires perturbations and transient runs. No numerical validation has been performed."
  },
